how do you find investors and partners  for your business if you're running our  business you can't do everything  yourself it's not possible  successful entrepreneurs do not do  everything themselves you're always  going to be limited by how much time you  have and you don't have the skillset the  experience or probably the desire to do  everything right you're really good at  one thing or two things but you're not  good at the hundred things that you need  to make your business successful and so  a great option is to look at bringing on  people bringing on a team either in the  form of employees but also partners to  help you make this business successful  finding a partner is like getting  married though it is topic is something  that you need to really invest a lot of  time with because you don't want to give  up a part of your business to somebody  who's not going to be a long-term fit  for your company I got a great question  from one of my readers Andy who wrote in  a long email he's an inventor he's  created this adventure in weightlifting  category so he's helping people could be  life saving invention for weight lifters  he's 52 years old he wants to retire  he's got this great invention  and he's looking for investors and  partners to help him take this thing to  the next level but he doesn't know where  to start there's nowhere to find these  people if you want to find somebody who  was a potential partner for you the best  thing you can do is start hanging around  in the circles that you are already  passionate about so if the product is  about weight lifting I don't know why  you started this business I'm assuming  your weight lifter right I hope your  weight lifter hope you know something  about this business I'm assuming you're  a passionate weight lifter you need to  start hanging around people who are also  passionate about weight lifter you can  hang around with at the gyms with gym  owners you can hang around with people  online who are in forms and communities  you can hang around if there's events  community events if there's trade shows  if there's conferences that's where you  need to be you need to be hanging around  people who care about weightlifting  because your goal here is to find people  who you can connect with who have the  same value system as you who believe in  the same things as you do who love the  idea of building a business but who have  complementary skills to what you do  you're the inventor  so you need to find somebody who's great  at sales and marketing we have a greater  production great at creating  distribution deals and those people  exist there are people who are great at  marketing who love weightlifting and who  share the same value system as you do  who want the same thing as a vision for  the business as you do and that's going  to come by hanging around in those  circles you're not going to have a lot  of success going posting online hey I  need a partner for this business right  that's not how you go out and find the  business partner it's got to be somebody  who is passionate about your community  just as much as you do you are believes  in the same thing that you do and define  those guys where are they going to hang  out you want to hang out where they're  hanging out and that's going to be at  the gyms and the trade shows and the  conferences and you don't have to be the  big schmoozer networking guy you know  hanging out you hanging out your cars  everybody doesn't have to be you but you  should start to get known a little bit  in your community for this great  invention that you have among the early  adopters right the people who love  trying new things and spread the word  that you're looking for a partner spread  the word that you are looking for some  marketing help and some investment help  that's how you're going to find those  initial first people to partner up with  or potential employees or potential  investors to your business here's an  example to kind of bring that home a  little bit more I this new guy on my  team okay his name is Jason he's been  helping me a lot with my branding and  web design and strategy a great new  person on the team and I met him because  I did an event for this coffee shop here  in Toronto what happened was a bus ran  into the coffee shop it something  happened it was trying to swerve away  from a bicyclist and the bus ran right  into a coffee shop smashed through the  front door the business had to go out of  business for a while to close down and  repair the shop and I knew the owner  I loved her coffee and her drinks and I  thought wow imagine how bad that is  imagine how bad it is to have a business  you're already struggling enough it's  hard enough to run a bit  this you have to worry about a bus  coming through your front door and  having to shut down for a couple weeks  and so I thought you know what I'm going  to surprise this business owner and I'm  going to send out a newsletter to my  list and say hey everybody let's meet at  this store on this date at this time  we'll have fun get to know each other  and and buy some coffee and some treats  and support this entrepreneur that's  something that's core to me that's  something that I believe in I believe in  helping entrepreneurs helping the little  guy and being a part of entrepreneurial  success that's what I love doing Jason  was a guy who came out to that event so  right away here is a guy who believes  the same thing as I do  he believes in entrepreneurs he wants to  help this person out there's something  about him that he shares that value with  me that would make us potentially  compatible people who got that email  might say as a stupid I'm not going to  go to this I got something else that day  I'm not going to make it a priority  that's great I don't want to talk to  those guys they're not going to be  potential fits for me I want someone  who's just as excited about this idea as  I am and that's what you need to find  for your business so Jason came out to  this event and we met we had coffee it  was great we met a couple times  afterwards we developed the relationship  we never thought about hey we should  work together it wasn't my intention  going in but we ended up working on some  projects and then he came on board and  became a bigger part of my team the same  thing can happen for you you've got to  go to events that you feel passionate  about and get involved in the  weightlifting community and people will  gravitate towards you the same people  who have the same value system and  believe in what you're doing they'll  come to you and you can decide who might  be a good potential partner and what  help you need to grow this thing up but  you're not going to find the partner by  just emailing people or by searching on  the web that's not how you do it you've  got to make real personal connections  with people who share the same system as  you same ideals and hopefully be able to  build a long-term relationship with them  it's a little bit what it's a little bit  scary it's a little bit not so concrete  and it may not work the first time you  know you can't go to one event and  expect something great to happen but if  you keep going eventually you'll find  the right people to help you take your  business to where it needs to go you  have to believe that it's going to work  at believe those are you watching liked  the video please give it a thumbs up  below and I'd love to hear what you have  to think leave a comment underneath let  me know your thoughts you have a  question leave it below make a video  response thank you so much and I'll see  you soon
 

